{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Beautiful, beautiful [C]brown eyes
[G]beautiful, beautiful [D7]brown eyes,
[G]Beautiful, beautiful [C]brown eyes;
I'll [D7]never love blue eyes [G]again.
Wille, I love you my darlin',
love you with all of my heart.
Tomorrow we might have been married,
but ramblin' has kept us apart.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Down through the bathroom he staggered,
and fell by the door.
The very last words he uttered,
I'll never see brown eyes no more.
{end_of_chorus}
